# The network of "Slow replication": the shop's app server, the site's
# firewall, the private link and the DR site.
#
#   app eth0 10.0.5.10 --- edge (inside 10.0.5.1 | outside 10.9.0.1) --- wan (10.9.0.2 | 10.0.6.1) --- dr 10.0.6.20
#
# wan is the private link, scenery: 50 Mbit/s towards dr and 50 ms each way.
# edge's idle timer, scenery too, stands for a managed firewall's: a
# connection quiet for 10 seconds is forgotten. wan routes the shop's own
# addresses back to edge, so only edge's firewall keeps the outside out.
machine app
machine edge router
machine wan router
machine dr

link app:eth0=10.0.5.10/24 edge:inside=10.0.5.1/24
link edge:outside=10.9.0.1/30 wan:edge=10.9.0.2/30
link wan:dr=10.0.6.1/24 dr:eth0=10.0.6.20/24

route app default via 10.0.5.1
route edge 10.0.6.0/24 via 10.9.0.2
route wan 10.0.5.0/24 via 10.9.0.1
route dr default via 10.0.6.1

sysctl edge net.netfilter.nf_conntrack_tcp_timeout_established=10

# The private link: towards dr, where the data goes, 50 Mbit/s and 50 ms;
# back towards edge, where the acknowledgements go, the 50 ms only.
netem wan dr rate 50mbit delay 50ms limit 2000
netem wan edge delay 50ms limit 2000

run edge nftables
run dr web-svc
